{"book":26,"chapter":27,"context":{"chapter":27,"title":"The Ship That Sank","summary":"Tyre is pictured as a magnificent merchant ship, built from the finest materials and loaded with goods from across the known world, that is wrecked on the high seas.","background":"The chapter is a funeral song (v. 2), and its long list of trading partners (vv. 12–25) is one of the richest descriptions of ancient commerce anywhere. It runs from Tarshish in the far west to Arabia and Mesopotamia, naming silver, tin, horses, ivory, spices, wool and slaves. Tyre's wealth depended on the sea, and the sea becomes its grave.","customs":[{"term":"Purple dye","verses":"27:7","note":"Tyre and its neighbors were famous for costly purple dye made from sea snails. Purple cloth signaled royalty and wealth."},{"term":"Tarshish ships","verses":"27:25","note":"Large ocean-going trading ships, named for the distant port of Tarshish, often placed in Spain."}],"watchFor":["The ship's parts: boards, mast, oars, sail (vv. 5–7).","The 'east wind' breaks it at sea (v. 26)."],"connections":["Revelation 18:11-19","Isaiah 23:8","1 Kings 10:22"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it came"],["דְבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] word of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]]},"2":{"w":[["וְאַתָּה","ve'atah","H859","HC/Pp2ms","and you"],["בֶן","ven-","H1121","HNcmsc","O son of"],["אָדָם","'adam","H120","HNcmsa","humankind"],["שָׂא","sa'","H5375","HVqv2ms","take up"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["צֹר","tzor","H6865","HNpl","Tyre"],["קִינָה","kinah","H7015","HNcfsa","a lamentation"]],"x":[[24009010,24009010,3],[24009017,24009020,3],[26019001,26019001,3],[26028012,26028012,3]],"xn":4},"3":{"w":[["וְאָמַרְתָּ","ve'amarta","H559","Hc/Vqq2ms","and you will say"],["לְצוֹר","letzor","H6865","HR/Npl","to Tyre"],["הַיֹּשֶׁבֶת","haiyoshevotei","H3427","HTd/Vqrfsa","that sits"],["עַ